%rec: default
#FIELDS: internal_name role identity icon routine
#
# One record per Townsperson. Everything here is data — no behaviour is
# hard-coded anywhere, and nobody needs an entry on the map to exist: a
# Townsperson the map does not already contain is spawned wherever their
# Schedule says they should be when the run begins.
#
#   role      one of: farmer smith builder trader authority
#   identity  who they are beneath the Role. Never shown to the player; it is
#             what their Private Actions are eventually written against.
#   icon      tile id in files/assets/classic_roguelike.png (row * 28 + col).
#             Optional, and only needed for people the map does not place.
#   routine   HH:MM-HH:MM activity place, where place is "x,y" or the name of a
#             location on the map. The Routine is the fixed part of the day and
#             reacts to nothing. Hours it leaves free are spare capacity, which
#             is what limits Reassignment later — so vary it deliberately.
#
# The original six and their days come from docs/specs/town-design-handover.md.
# Places are named rather than numbered: the names come from WAYPOINTS in
# scripts/build_town.py, which writes them onto the map's Meta layer.
#
# The town's trades, and who feeds whom, are in obligations.rec. Read the two
# together: this file is where people are, that one is what they owe.

internal_name: elias
role: farmer
identity: has a daughter in the cemetery and has told no one how often he goes
routine: 22:00-05:00 sleep farmer_bedroom
routine: 05:00-06:00 meal farmhouse
routine: 07:00-10:00 harvest vegetable_field
routine: 12:00-13:00 lunch lunch_tree
routine: 13:00-16:00 harvest grain_field
routine: 19:00-20:00 meal farmhouse
routine: 21:00-22:00 home farmhouse

internal_name: martin
role: farmer
identity: wakes on the riverbank with no memory of walking there
routine: 23:00-02:00 sleep miller_bedroom
routine: 03:00-06:00 sleep miller_bedroom
routine: 06:00-07:00 meal mill_interior
routine: 07:00-10:00 grind mill
routine: 12:00-13:00 lunch river
routine: 13:00-17:00 grind mill
routine: 17:00-18:00 waterwheel river
routine: 19:00-23:00 home mill_interior

internal_name: greta
role: trader
identity: has been thinning the ale since the bad winter and cannot stop now
routine: 23:00-05:00 sleep innkeeper_bedroom
routine: 05:00-07:00 kitchen inn
routine: 07:00-11:00 serve inn
routine: 13:00-17:00 serve inn
routine: 18:00-19:00 serve inn
routine: 20:00-22:00 clean inn

internal_name: otto
role: smith
identity: keeps every scrap of iron anyone throws away and will not say why
routine: 22:00-06:00 sleep blacksmith_bedroom
routine: 06:00-07:00 meal blacksmith
routine: 07:00-12:00 forge blacksmith
routine: 13:00-17:00 forge blacksmith
routine: 20:00-22:00 home blacksmith_bedroom

internal_name: marta
role: builder
identity: carves toys for a child who is not hers and never gives them away
routine: 23:00-06:00 sleep carpenter_bedroom
routine: 06:00-07:00 meal carpenter_workshop
routine: 07:00-11:00 workshop carpenter_workshop
routine: 13:00-17:00 workshop carpenter_workshop
routine: 19:00-21:00 workshop carpenter_interior

internal_name: aldren
role: authority
identity: lost his faith years ago and has been reading his belief off paper since
routine: 22:00-05:00 sleep priest_bedroom
routine: 05:00-06:00 prayer church
routine: 06:00-07:00 meal priest_study
routine: 09:00-11:00 duties church
routine: 13:00-17:00 visits town_square
routine: 19:00-20:00 prayer church

# Jorin keeps the animals: the milk, the eggs and the muscle the fields need
# that Elias no longer has. He is up before anyone and in the fields with the
# farmer every afternoon, which makes him the one person whose day touches both
# ends of the town's food.
internal_name: jorin
role: farmer
identity: came to the farm as a boy after a winter he does not talk about
icon: 342
routine: 21:00-04:00 sleep hayloft
routine: 04:00-05:30 animals barn
routine: 10:00-12:00 grazing pasture
routine: 12:00-13:00 lunch lunch_tree
routine: 13:00-16:00 harvest grain_field
routine: 17:30-18:30 herd pasture
routine: 19:00-20:00 animals barn
routine: 20:00-21:00 meal farmhouse

# Bram works the river, which is the town's one food supply that owes nothing
# to the weather on the fields. He is also the furthest from everybody — out of
# sight for most of the day, and missed slowly.
internal_name: bram
role: farmer
identity: keeps a second line in the water that he never baits
icon: 457
routine: 23:00-05:00 sleep fisher_bedroom
routine: 05:00-08:00 fishing fishing_spot
routine: 12:00-13:00 meal inn
routine: 14:00-18:00 fishing fishing_spot
routine: 19:00-20:00 meal fisher_cottage

# Hilde sells. Nothing she handles is hers: it comes in off the farm, the river
# and the mill in the morning and goes out across her counter all day. Kill the
# people who produce and her stall is bare; kill her and the producers have
# nowhere to put what they grow.
internal_name: hilde
role: trader
identity: counts the takings twice and writes the smaller number down
icon: 314
routine: 22:00-05:30 sleep trader_bedroom
routine: 06:00-07:00 meal trader_house
routine: 08:00-12:00 stall market_stall
routine: 13:00-17:00 stall market_stall
routine: 19:00-20:00 meal inn
routine: 20:00-22:00 evening inn
